test - evaluate a file, string or integer condition

SYNOPSIS
    test expression
    [ expression ]

DESCRIPTION
    An empty expression is false. A single string is true if nonempty.
    Use -e, -f, -d, -r, -w and -x for files, -n and -z for strings,
    = and != to compare strings, and -eq, -ne, -lt, -le, -gt or -ge
    for signed integers. A leading ! reverses a condition.
    Exit 0 for true, 1 for false and 2 for invalid expressions.

EXAMPLES
    if [ -r "$HOME" ]; then echo readable; fi

SEE ALSO
    sh(1)
